INFRASTRUCTURE OBSERVATIONS — Round 5 specifics
================================================================

Cargo registry zombies
  23 zombie cargo/rustc procs from PRIOR sessions (7-9 hours old,
  some in U-state) were holding ~/.cargo/registry lock, slowing every
  agent's pre-commit hook. xargs kill cleared them once they exited
  U-state.

Hung bv (10-hour TUI)
  PID 14688 was a leftover `bv` TUI from a session that started 10
  hours earlier. It held `.beads/issues.jsonl` open via FD 19r,
  blocking `bd sync --flush-only` (which runs inside every pre-commit
  hook) for 7+ minutes per commit. Killed via `kill -KILL 14688`;
  immediately freed cc_2's chore-commit hook + the whole queue.
  Per skill: NEVER run bare `bv`; always use `--robot-*` flags.

Pre-commit auto-stager (memory-confirmed)
  ADR 0049 was written by cc_4 but never explicitly committed by cc_4
  — it was SWEPT IN to cc_3's 9f36bbbc commit by the pre-commit
  auto-stager. AGENTS.md memory `pre_commit_hook_sweeps_staged_files`
  noted this pattern; Round 5 saw it produce a (benign) cross-bead
  commit grouping. Bead-close was still honest because the ADR
  actually shipped to origin/main.

ntm send-keys vs paste-buffer
  Multi-line dispatch via `tmux send-keys "$CONTENT"` truncates
  silently when text contains special chars; `tmux load-buffer +
  paste-buffer` triggers Claude Code's Rewind UI. Round 5's resilient
  pattern: short single-line plain-text via send-keys with heavy
  inter-pane stagger (4s+) to evade anthropic-side parallel
  rate-limits.

